    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0355" n="343" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg343"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.24/25a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Farrell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-01T17:00:00-04:00">May 1, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. The President will announce on May 2 that Iraq has been designated as
                    eligible to receive Lend-Lease assistance.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d401-f1"/>
                    Please inform Iraqi Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d401-f1" n="6" xml:id="d401-f1-content">
                <p>For the text of announcement concerning lend-lease aid to both Iraq and Iran, see
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, May 2, 1942, p. 383;
                    for correspondence regarding lend-lease aid to Iran, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg289">pp. 289</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
